  "conclusion": "The original 4x256KiB Hyle loss remains after matching the socket seam. Two matched points are slower by about13-15%; this is not a stable universal percentage. Peer absolute time changes along with the libc seam; unchanged Hyle also varies. Small body still faster in this narrow workload. Do not claim the seam explained or solved the product residual.",
  "clock": "Raw min epoch windows are milliseconds and empirical resolution12-16ns. Counter fields zero mean unavailable, not no CPU work. Process and order drift are not clock quantization.",
